d value equality.\n\nHmm, but wait: does `_apply_animation_item` update base positions via `handle.update_positions`? Yes. And normals for base mesh: no update API → static → exact equality via topology fields. Good.\n\nBut hold on — there's a subtlety with the base mesh in `_animation_mesh_compatible`: `_ANIMATION_VALUE_FIELDS` uses `_value_shapes_compatible` which allows None transitions. For chunks, `_arrays_equal(None, x)` returns False unless both None. So a chunk going from None displacements to arrays would be incompatible → rebuild. That's conservative and correct (no granular mutation API).\n\nAlso check: does `handle.chunks` return list of (chunk_id, mesh)? In `_animation_item_compatible`: `for (chunk_id, chunk, _owners, _resolver), (current_id, current) in zip(chunks, existing)` — yes, existing is `handle.chunks` yielding (id, mesh) pairs.\n\nNow, does the oracle test 1 pass with this? Test: view.add_mesh_arrays(mesh()) — base mesh. handle.add_chunk('part', mesh()). begin_animation_cache, capture frame 0. handle.replace_chunk('part', mesh(shift=.25, value=7.)). capture frame 1. Show frame 0 (rebuild path since _animation_handles empty → full rebuild, handles created). Show frame 1: `_update_animation_handles(frame1)`: base mesh compatible (unchanged), chunk 'part': positions changed → `_animation_chunk_compatible` False → return False → full rebuild → new handle with new chunk mesh. Then `view._animation_handles[0].chunks['part']` has new positions/scalars. \n\nTest 2 (normals): base mesh normals changed between frames. `_animation_mesh_compatible`: normals in topology fields → not equal → incompatible → full rebuild → new normals. \n\nWait, but in test 2, the test directly mutates `view._animation_cache[1]['meshes'][0]['mesh'] = mesh(normal=-1.)`. Frame 1's mesh has different normals. Show frame 0 → rebuild. Show frame 1 → incompatible (normals differ) → rebuild → handle.mesh.normals == new. \n\nAlso `handle.mesh` — is that the MeshArrays? `view._animation_handles[0].mesh.normals` — yes.\n\n3. Scheduler drain fail-fast fix.\n\n4. `_UpdateNotifier.wake`: reset `_pending` if postEvent raises:\n\n```python\ndef wake(self):\n    with self._wake_lock:\n        if self._pending:\n            return\n        self._pending = True\n    try:\n        QCoreApplication.postEvent(self, _UpdateEvent())\n    except Exception:\n        with self._wake_lock:\n            self._pending = False\n        raise\n```\n\nNow, the focused regressions to complete:\n- update old pump tests (tests/test_qt_update_pump.py) for no idle timer, bounded/coalesced owner-thread delivery/cancel/failure\n- testGPU16ms latestevent (GPU hover 16ms bounded interval, latest event)\n- software prep invalidation/eviction\n- compatible base-animation handle identity and incompatible fallback\n- selection cache reuse after scalar and invalidation geometry\n- Existing fake software harness needs bindings for new helpers.\n\nLet me look at the existing test files: tests/test_qt_update_pump.py, tests/test_scheduler.py, and check if tests/test_performance_improvements.py exists. Also run_check.py to know how to run tests.", "summary": []}
